00:05:15.715 --> 00:05:17.584
- [Voiceover] Taylor asks, 
"How does the startup know

00:05:17.584 --> 00:05:18.752
"when to add staff?

00:05:18.752 --> 00:05:21.555
"What positions are most
critical to line up first?"

00:05:21.555 --> 00:05:24.157
- Taylor, and by the way before
I get into your answer Taylor,

00:05:24.157 --> 00:05:27.894
obviously this is a startup
themed episode in honor of the

00:05:27.894 --> 00:05:29.829
43North competition.

00:05:29.829 --> 00:05:34.533
Taylor, I think that there's a
lot of ways to go about this.

00:05:34.533 --> 00:05:37.504
I think you reverse engineer
the founders of the company.

00:05:37.504 --> 00:05:39.406
So there's a lot of
things that are needed.

00:05:39.406 --> 00:05:41.741
Financial understanding 
is needed.

00:05:41.741 --> 00:05:43.076
Marketing understanding
is needed.

00:05:43.076 --> 00:05:45.011
Product understanding 
is needed.

00:05:45.011 --> 00:05:46.980
There's a lot of needs
when you're a small company.

00:05:46.980 --> 00:05:50.951
I think what you need to 
do is first you hire as soon

00:05:50.951 --> 00:05:52.828
as you can afford to.

00:05:52.828 --> 00:05:55.655
There are startups that I know
that are literally paying their

00:05:55.655 --> 00:05:59.159
founders and CEOs way too much
money because they want to take

00:05:59.159 --> 00:05:59.993
the money home.

00:05:59.993 --> 00:06:03.563
You've got to start spending it
to invest in your business but

00:06:03.563 --> 00:06:04.731
not more than you have.

00:06:04.731 --> 00:06:07.867
So if you make 30 
or $40,000 a year as an

00:06:07.867 --> 00:06:08.835
entrepreneur that's plenty.

00:06:08.835 --> 00:06:10.537
You're building an asset 
for yourself for the

00:06:10.537 --> 00:06:11.771
rest of your life.

00:06:11.771 --> 00:06:14.874
It's better than making 100 so
you can take that 70,000 and go

00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:18.552
and hire your head of marketing,
hire a project manager,

00:06:18.552 --> 00:06:20.380
hire whatever needs you have.

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:23.149
Who to hire is actually
quite easy my opinion.

00:06:23.149 --> 00:06:27.854
You hire around the thing that
you most need that you yourself

00:06:27.854 --> 00:06:29.189
can't most provide.

00:06:29.189 --> 00:06:32.392
I don't hire salespeople
very quickly in my companies.

00:06:32.392 --> 00:06:35.718
I don't hire HR
people very quickly.

00:06:35.718 --> 00:06:39.499
We didn't have a HR department
or a sales staff for the first

00:06:39.499 --> 00:06:42.302
five of the seven years of
VaynerMedia and everyboy thought

00:06:42.302 --> 00:06:44.804
that was so crazy because
those of the things that I did.

00:06:44.804 --> 00:06:46.940
Those are things that I
could do with my hustle.

00:06:46.940 --> 00:06:51.311
But we did have a CFO and a
legal person very quickly over

00:06:51.311 --> 00:06:53.747
our means because
those were shortcomings.

00:06:53.747 --> 00:06:56.983
I think AJ could have probably
learned it on the job but those

00:06:56.983 --> 00:06:58.485
are things we
didn't have as much of.

00:06:58.485 --> 00:07:01.554
I think when you hire first is
the thing you need to round out

00:07:01.554 --> 00:07:03.556
your team with even if it's not.

00:07:03.556 --> 00:07:08.995
Let's say sales is more
important than legal but you're

00:07:08.995 --> 00:07:13.300
great at sales I think you still
fix legal even though it's less

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:16.202
in priority because by doubling
down on a person you're still

00:07:16.202 --> 00:07:18.972
zero here and you might just
gain 20 to 50 percent here,

00:07:18.972 --> 00:07:21.841
where maybe your hustle 
and your efforts could just

00:07:21.841 --> 00:07:23.677
be the part that gains.

00:07:23.677 --> 00:07:26.212
I think that sometimes people
say sales of the number one

00:07:26.212 --> 00:07:27.981
thing for this company but even
though I'm great in sales I'm

00:07:27.981 --> 00:07:31.051
gonna hire second person and
won't get to that I find that to

00:07:31.051 --> 00:07:31.818
